Subject: [PATCH 2/5] NEXA-451: prepare the server UI dist before staging a git
 payload

`paperclipai install --repo <owner/name> --ref <branch>` could not build a
payload at all: the server package ships the built UI inside it, and
prepare-bundled-package.mjs copies server/ui-dist into the staged package.
A fresh git checkout has no server/ui-dist -- it is produced by
scripts/prepare-server-ui-dist.sh, which the server package's own prepack
hook runs, and prepack only runs on `pnpm pack`. This flow stages the server
package directly, so the hook never fires and the packaging step died with

    Error: ENOENT: no such file or directory, lstat '.../source/server/ui-dist'

after the whole build had already run (~20 minutes).

Build the UI before the workspace packages are staged, the same way
scripts/release.sh does it before it packs. Without this, a fork branch
cannot be installed on an instance at all, which is the only supported way
to ship a fork build, and the managed install store's git source cannot be
used.

Test: cli/src/__tests__/install-command.test.ts now asserts the UI
preparation runs, and that it runs before prepare-bundled-package.mjs
stages the bundled package.
