From 77b24b218c0a1897043b353759f9f130c3803e4c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jjude80 <18168364+jjude80@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 23:05:32 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] NEXA-424: keep a refused child out of the holder's
 checkout

A review found a hole in the refusal: refusing the reuse of another issue's
isolated workspace is not enough on its own. A child that carries a pinned
workspaceStrategy.existingBranch still realizes into the holder's checkout,
because realization finds the worktree registered for that branch and reuses
it. The run was refused a workspace and then given the same tree by another
door.

The dispatch path now drops the pinned branch when the reuse was refused
because the workspace belongs to another issue, so the child derives its own
branch and its own worktree. The strategy config is resolved through
resolveExecutionWorkspaceStrategyConfig, which the workspace preparation uses
for the effective run config, the plugin preparation and the realization.

Also removes the code comments this branch added: CONTRIBUTING.md says "Do not
submit a PR that includes code comments." The reasoning moves to the pull
request description.

Tests: execution-workspace-policy covers the strategy resolution (a pinned
branch is dropped for a foreign owner, kept for the issue's own workspace, and
the whole strategy is dropped when the branch was all it held);
heartbeat-workspace-session covers the dispatch path, from the refusal through
the effective strategy the run realizes with.
