From 1746a280dd149c0dd5af37f03a6c21dfa9fd251d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jjude80 <18168364+jjude80@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 04:47:03 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] NEXA-432: skip the managed credential broker for
 local-only Git commands

Every `git` invocation on an agent's PATH went through the managed GitHub
launcher, which asked the control plane for managed credentials before each
call, including calls that never touch the network. The round trip cost about
1.8s per command, so a local-only script (the 127-case worktree suite, the
pre-commit hook calling `git rev-parse`) took over ten minutes instead of
forty seconds, and timed out the gates that depend on it. A timeout is
reported as a failing test, so a green suite turned red for a reason that had
nothing to do with the change under test.

The launcher now recognises the Git commands that cannot reach a remote and
cannot create a commit object, and skips the broker round trip for them.
Commands that contact a remote keep it, and so do commands that create
commits: the broker is what supplies the managed identity that commits are
attributed to, and the credential helper that authenticates a push.

Measured in this repository, five `git rev-parse HEAD` calls: 10.6s before,
1.4s after. A local command also no longer reports a broker diagnostic it
cannot have; the diagnostic still appears on the commands that need a
credential.

Co-Authored-By: Paperclip <noreply@paperclip.ing>
